WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.872
This query distinguishes NULL from blank text.

00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:08.292
COUNT column ignores NULL values but still counts empty strings.

00:00:08.292 --> 00:00:16.542
COUNT of NULLIF BTRIM column comma empty string excludes both NULL and blank-after-trimming values.

00:00:16.542 --> 00:00:20.687
Run the query and compare the non-null and non-blank counts.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:24.772
That difference is an important part of completeness profiling.

00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:28.277
Missingness has several representations: NULL, blank text, whitespace,

00:00:28.277 --> 00:00:33.312
and sometimes sentinel codes such as Unknown or 999.

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:37.317
Do not collapse them blindly.

00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:42.192
First decide whether they mean the same thing in the source system,

00:00:42.192 --> 00:00:46.955
then normalize deliberately and keep lineage when the original value may matter.
